# Reusable stats panel and unit-card popover plan

This checklist is the implementation source of truth for the following open
item in `docs/project.todo`:

> Add a SoulSearch "stats view" modal-window popover to the base game's unit
> card window, so users can inspect a unit without opening the full SoulSearch
> window.

The work has two inseparable parts:

1. encapsulate the existing Stats panel as a behavior-complete reusable
   component; and
2. use that component in a new popover opened from a DFHack overlay button on
   the vanilla unit card.

Do not mark the parent `docs/project.todo` item complete until every automated
gate and the final live fortress-mode gate in this document has passed.

Record phase results in the `Execution evidence` table at the end of this
document. Every completed phase gate must have a dated entry that identifies
the commands, tests, screenshots/observations, or live fortress checks that
justify marking it complete.

## Target behavior

- [ ] The main SoulSearch window and the unit-card popover instantiate the same
      reusable Stats component.
- [ ] The shared component owns its views, relative layout, rendered records,
      scrolling behavior, sort interaction, hit-testing, and stats tooltips.
- [ ] The main window preserves its current Stats geometry and behavior.
- [ ] A visible SoulSearch button appears only on the vanilla fortress-mode
      unit card (`dwarfmode/ViewSheets/UNIT`).
- [ ] Activating the button captures the unit currently displayed by the
      vanilla card and opens a compact modal Stats popover for that unit.
- [ ] The popover does not open the results list, filter editor, presets, or any
      other part of the full SoulSearch window.
- [ ] Closing the popover returns the player to the same vanilla unit card.

## Architectural constraints

- [ ] Add functionality through DFHack's overlay framework; do not modify or
      retain references to the vanilla unit card's internal widget tree.
- [ ] Capture the selected `df.unit` before showing the new
      `gui.ZScreenModal`.
      Selection lookup must not depend on the popover already being on top.
- [ ] Snapshot only the selected unit when opening the popover. Do not collect
      or search every fortress candidate for a single-unit stats view.
- [ ] Keep `stats_presenter.lua` responsible for presentation records and
      formatted content; do not duplicate attribute evaluation or formatting
      in the popover.
- [ ] Define a narrow `SoulSearchStatsSubject` data contract for Stats hosts:
      `unit`, `row`, `name`, `profession`, and `filter_criteria`. Normal search
      results must satisfy it structurally, while the popover constructs one
      directly from its captured unit.
- [ ] Keep reusable column dimensions and hitbox boundaries in a dependency-
      free `stats_layout.lua`. `ui_format.lua` and `stats_panel.lua` may both
      consume it; neither may import the other.
- [ ] Keep sort validation, defaults, and next-state transitions in a pure
      `stats_sort.lua` module shared by all hosts.
- [ ] Keep sort persistence outside the reusable component. The component may
      own active sort interaction state, but reports changes through a callback
      so each host decides whether and where to save them.
- [ ] Treat programmatic `set_sort(sort)` as silent. Invoke
      `on_sort_change(sort)` only for a user-initiated sort transition, avoiding
      persistence callbacks during initialization or host refresh.
- [ ] Keep main-window settings and popover settings independent. Opening or
      sorting the popover must not silently mutate the default SoulSearch
      window's saved settings.
- [ ] Keep tooltip rendering at screen level so it can escape panel clipping.
      The reusable Stats component should expose its current tooltip text to
      either host screen.
- [ ] Extract the screen-level tooltip renderer into `ui_tooltip.lua` with a
      host-agnostic `get_tooltip_text() -> string` owner contract. Use an empty
      string, not `nil`, when no tooltip is active.
- [ ] Register every new internal module in `module_registry.lua` and in the
      pure-Lua test harness where required.
- [ ] Register every SoulSearch-owned popover screen with `screen_registry.lua`
      so `soulsearch reload` and teardown dismiss it safely.
- [ ] Make popover registration and dismissal idempotent across explicit close,
      `onDismiss`, `onDestroy`, reload, and invalid-unit failure paths.
- [ ] Do not let the overlay widget retain a stale local reference to a
      reloadable popover module. Resolve the popover entry point dynamically on
      activation, or make `soulsearch reload` rescan/reconstruct the overlay
      widget before reuse.

## Phase 0 - Baseline and vanilla integration proof

- [ ] Record the current main-window Stats behavior before refactoring:
  - [ ] title, underline, unit name, profession, and selected-filter summary;
  - [ ] physical, mental, and trait color categories;
  - [ ] omission of stats that do not deviate meaningfully from baseline;
  - [ ] fixed `Stat` and `Delta` header with independently scrolling rows;
  - [ ] stat-name and delta sort cycles and their current default directions;
  - [ ] stat-name, sort-header, and delta tooltips;
  - [ ] correct tooltip record after scrolling via `start_line_num`; and
  - [ ] empty/no-selection behavior.
- [ ] In a current fortress, verify and record the vanilla unit-card focus
      string with `dfhack.gui.getFocusStrings()`.
- [ ] Verify `dfhack.gui.getSelectedUnit(true)` returns the unit displayed on
      `dwarfmode/ViewSheets/UNIT` before any SoulSearch screen is shown.
- [ ] Verify a module-loadable script under `scripts_modinstalled` can register
      an `OVERLAY_WIDGETS` entry and constrain it to the unit-card focus path.
- [ ] Verify `gui.ZScreenModal` pauses and blocks input as expected when opened
      from both paused and unpaused unit cards, and record the intended pause
      restoration behavior after dismissal.
- [ ] Record a safe default overlay-button position at the supported UI scales
      and minimum practical game resolution.
- [ ] Run the existing automated baseline before source changes:
  - [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Test.ps1`; and
  - [ ] `git diff --check`.

### Phase 0 gate

- [ ] The unit-card focus, selected-unit lookup, overlay discovery, default
      placement, and current Stats behavior are evidence-backed rather than
      assumed.
- [ ] Existing automated gates are green before the extraction begins.

## Phase 1 - Characterize the reusable behavior seam

- [ ] Expand characterization coverage for all behavior moving out of
      `ui.lua`, `ui_components.lua`, and `ui_layout.lua`:
  - [ ] view composition and stable child IDs;
  - [ ] dynamic header/columns/body layout;
  - [ ] label and delta column boundaries;
  - [ ] the three-state sort cycle for both columns;
  - [ ] sort defaults and reverse-direction rules;
  - [ ] display-record retention, including section gaps;
  - [ ] header, delta, and attribute tooltip selection; and
  - [ ] scrolled-row tooltip indexing;
  - [ ] relayout after the host frame changes without requiring
        `set_subject()`; and
  - [ ] silent programmatic sort updates versus callback-producing user sort
        actions.
- [ ] Add a focused single-unit adapter API, such as
      `residents.collect_unit(unit)`, that constructs a
      `SoulSearchStatsSubject` without scanning a candidate scope.
- [ ] Add tests for units with:
  - [ ] physical, mental, and personality data;
  - [ ] no current soul;
  - [ ] no meaningful deviations; and
  - [ ] missing or fallback display names.
- [ ] Define and document the `SoulSearchStatsSubject` contract, including an
      empty `filter_criteria` sequence for unit-card subjects and structural
      compatibility with normal SoulSearch results.
- [ ] Add characterization tests for the current resident-specific empty and
      fallback strings, then decide whether shared Stats copy should use the
      generic term `unit` or accept host-supplied terminology. Record the choice
      before supporting visitors and animals in the popover.
- [ ] Extract pure sort normalization and transition tests from
      `window_config.lua` and `ui.lua` into the planned `stats_sort.lua` seam.

### Phase 1 gate

- [ ] Tests fail if the extraction changes existing sort, hitbox, tooltip,
      scrolling, formatting, or empty-state behavior.
- [ ] Single-unit stats data can be constructed without running a full search.

## Phase 2 - Extract the reusable Stats component

- [ ] Add a focused internal module, preferably `stats_panel.lua`, containing a
      `widgets.Panel`-derived reusable component.
- [ ] Add dependency-free `stats_layout.lua` before moving layout constants:
  - [ ] move reusable label width, value-column position, and hitbox boundaries
        into it;
  - [ ] update `ui_format.lua` to consume it; and
  - [ ] keep main-window placement coordinates in `ui_layout.lua`.
- [ ] Add pure `stats_sort.lua` and make the component, window configuration,
      and tests consume its default, normalization, and next-state helpers.
- [ ] Extract `SoulSearchTooltip` into `ui_tooltip.lua` without importing
      `ui.lua` or depending on `SoulSearchWindow`.
- [ ] Give the component a small host-facing API:
  - [ ] initial `subject` and `sort` attributes;
  - [ ] `set_subject(subject)`;
  - [ ] `set_sort(sort)`;
  - [ ] `get_sort()`;
  - [ ] `get_tooltip_text()`; and
  - [ ] `on_sort_change(sort)` callback.
- [ ] Move Stats-owned view creation into the component:
  - [ ] title and underline;
  - [ ] unit header;
  - [ ] fixed column header; and
  - [ ] scrollable stats body.
- [ ] Convert Stats layout from main-window absolute coordinates to
      component-relative coordinates.
- [ ] Recompute component-relative frames and hitboxes when the component's
      current `frame_body` changes, independently of data refresh.
- [ ] Preserve the current text column geometry and click boundaries unless a
      separately recorded live incompatibility requires a deliberate change.
- [ ] Move Stats-owned behavior into the component:
  - [ ] presentation refresh and `stats_records` retention;
  - [ ] sort-column hit-testing and sort cycling;
  - [ ] attribute-row and delta-cell hit-testing; and
  - [ ] header, attribute, and delta tooltip selection.
- [ ] Continue using `stats_presenter.lua` as the sole producer of Stats text
      and display records.
- [ ] Keep screen-sized tooltip positioning and painting outside the component.
- [ ] Remove obsolete Stats construction/update helpers from
      `ui_components.lua` after both behavior and tests have moved.
- [ ] Move component-internal constants and hit-testing out of the main-window
      `ui_layout.lua`; keep only the component's placement frame there and put
      shared formatting geometry in `stats_layout.lua`.
- [ ] Register the module and update loader-contract tests.

### Phase 2 gate

- [ ] The component can be instantiated in an arbitrary parent frame without
      referring to `STATS_LEFT`, the main window, result-list subviews, or
      `window_settings`.
- [ ] Component tests cover rendering state, sorting, layout, scrolling, and
      tooltips without constructing the full SoulSearch screen.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 3 - Migrate the main SoulSearch window

- [ ] Replace the existing five loose Stats views with one reusable Stats
      component positioned at the current Stats panel location.
- [ ] Route `ui_refresh.lua` Stats refreshes to
      `stats_panel:set_subject(result)`.
- [ ] Initialize the component from the current window identity's saved
      `stats_sort` snapshot.
- [ ] Persist sort changes through the component callback using the existing
      window-settings path.
- [ ] Make the main tooltip aggregator ask the Stats component for Stats-owned
      tooltip text while preserving the priority of unrelated control,
      results, filter, and picker tooltips.
- [ ] Render the aggregated tooltip through the shared `ui_tooltip.lua`
      screen-level view.
- [ ] Remove superseded Stats fields and methods from `SoulSearchWindow`,
      including duplicated sort, hit-test, tooltip, and refresh ownership.
- [ ] Preserve the current Stats panel placement, width, height, divider,
      header behavior, and scroll extent at the default window size.
- [ ] Preserve live resizing behavior and refresh the component layout from its
      own current `frame_body`.

### Phase 3 gate

- [ ] No main-window Stats rendering or interaction path bypasses the reusable
      component.
- [ ] Existing tests pass with the full-window callers migrated.
- [ ] Live fortress smoke confirms unchanged main-window geometry, sorting,
      scrolling, hover text, selection refresh, resizing, and saved sort state.

## Phase 4 - Implement the single-unit Stats popover

- [ ] Add a dedicated popover module and `gui.ZScreenModal` implementation
      rather than invoking `ui.open()` for the full SoulSearch window.
- [ ] Construct the selected unit's `SoulSearchStatsSubject` through the Phase
      1 single-unit adapter.
- [ ] Instantiate the reusable Stats component as the popover's content.
- [ ] Give the popover a compact, clamped frame that remains usable at the
      minimum supported game window size.
- [ ] Add a dedicated `stats_popover_config.lua`, or a generic reusable frame-
      normalization helper, for popover defaults and screen-bound clamping. Do
      not reuse the main window's private 90x30 normalization contract.
- [ ] Add an explicit close control and normal `Esc`/right-click dismissal.
- [ ] Rely on `gui.ZScreenModal` for modal input and pause behavior so clicks do
      not activate controls on the vanilla card underneath it.
- [ ] Add a shared `ui_tooltip.lua` screen-level sibling driven by
      `stats_panel:get_tooltip_text()`.
- [ ] Define popover sort state as independent from the main window:
  - [ ] initialize it from documented popover defaults;
  - [ ] retain it for the lifetime of the popover; and
  - [ ] do not write it to the default SoulSearch window identity.
- [ ] Register and unregister the popover through `screen_registry.lua`.
- [ ] Route explicit close, `onDismiss`, and `onDestroy` through one idempotent
      cleanup path that unregisters the screen exactly once.
- [ ] Handle invalid or stale units gracefully without leaving a broken screen
      on the viewscreen stack.
- [ ] Add pure-Lua tests for result construction, default sort, callbacks,
      close behavior, and teardown bookkeeping where the harness can model it.

### Phase 4 gate

- [ ] The popover renders through the same Stats component used by the main
      window and contains no copied Stats formatting, sort, hit-test, scrolling,
      or tooltip logic.
- [ ] Popover construction requires only the captured unit and popover options;
      it does not depend on a live `SoulSearchWindow`.

## Phase 5 - Add the vanilla unit-card overlay button

- [ ] Add a side-effect-free, module-loadable overlay registration script.
- [ ] Define a global `OVERLAY_WIDGETS` entry backed by
      `overlay.OverlayWidget`.
- [ ] Choose and document a stable `OVERLAY_WIDGETS` key/widget identity. Set
      its overlay configuration version deliberately, and increment it only
      when intentionally resetting saved placement/configuration is required.
- [ ] Restrict `viewscreens` to the confirmed fortress-mode unit-card focus
      path instead of all of `dwarfmode`.
- [ ] Make the overlay enabled by default for first-time SoulSearch users while
      allowing normal disable/reposition control through DFHack.
- [ ] Render a clearly branded, compact SoulSearch Stats button at the recorded
      safe default position.
- [ ] On activation:
  - [ ] call `dfhack.gui.getSelectedUnit(true)` before showing a new screen;
  - [ ] do nothing unsafe and report a concise error if no unit is available;
  - [ ] pass the captured unit to the popover API; and
  - [ ] return or track the owned screen according to DFHack overlay lifecycle
        requirements.
- [ ] Resolve the popover module with `reqscript()` at activation time, or use
      an equivalently reload-safe lookup, so `soulsearch reload` cannot leave
      the widget calling a stale module table.
- [ ] Ensure the overlay widget itself is never attached as a popover subview.
- [ ] Avoid per-tick unit scanning or Stats recomputation in overlay callbacks.
- [ ] Add registration, focus-path, default-state, activation, and missing-unit
      tests with overlay/GUI stubs.
- [ ] Document the development reload procedure:
      `:lua require('plugins.overlay').rescan()` after script changes.
- [ ] Define the production `soulsearch reload` behavior explicitly:
  - [ ] dismiss all registered main and popover screens;
  - [ ] reload internal modules;
  - [ ] rescan the overlay if the widget captures reloadable state; and
  - [ ] prove the next button activation uses the current popover code.

### Phase 5 gate

- [ ] `overlay list` discovers the widget and `gui/control-panel` can enable or
      disable it.
- [ ] The button appears on the vanilla unit card and nowhere outside its
      confirmed focus context.
- [ ] Activating it always opens Stats for the unit that was visible at click
      time.

## Phase 6 - Automated integration, packaging, and documentation

- [ ] Update `tests/run.lua`, the module registry, and test support loaders for
      every new suite and internal module.
- [ ] Update README/help text to describe:
  - [ ] the unit-card Stats button;
  - [ ] overlay enable/disable and reposition behavior; and
  - [ ] the relationship between the compact popover and full SoulSearch.
- [ ] Ensure the source and packaged mod contain the overlay registration and
      every runtime dependency.
- [ ] Run the automated closure sequence separately:
  - [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Test.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Publish.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1`; and
  - [ ] `git diff --check`.
- [ ] Record production Lua count, test count, package path, and all command
      results in this document when the phase is executed.

### Phase 6 gate

- [ ] Syntax, pure-Lua behavior, package contents, documentation, and whitespace
      checks are green.
- [ ] Automated success is not treated as proof of live overlay placement,
      focus, input, or rendering behavior.

## Phase 7 - Live fortress-mode acceptance

### Main-window regression

- [ ] Open the full SoulSearch window and confirm results selection still
      refreshes the shared Stats component.
- [ ] Confirm name, profession, selected-filter summary, colors, deviations,
      separators, and empty states match the Phase 0 baseline.
- [ ] Exercise all three states of both Stats sort headers.
- [ ] Scroll the Stats body and verify attribute tooltips continue to describe
      the row under the mouse, not the pre-scroll row.
- [ ] Verify the delta and header tooltips at both edges and immediately outside
      their hitboxes.
- [ ] Resize, drag, close, and reopen the full window; verify Stats layout and
      saved sort behavior remain intact.

### Overlay and popover acceptance

- [ ] Confirm the overlay is listed, enabled by default on first registration,
      and configurable through `gui/control-panel` and `gui/overlay`.
- [ ] Open vanilla unit cards from every practical entry route and confirm the
      button appears consistently.
- [ ] Confirm the button does not appear on item sheets, the creatures list,
      the main map, or unrelated information tabs.
- [ ] Open the popover for several units and verify each captured identity,
      profession, attributes, traits, deviations, and colors are current.
- [ ] Include at least:
  - [ ] a normal citizen with a current soul;
  - [ ] a non-citizen or visitor accessible from a unit card;
  - [ ] an animal or other unit without a current soul; and
  - [ ] a unit with few or no meaningful deviations.
- [ ] Exercise sorting, scrolling, stat-name tooltips, header tooltips, and
      delta tooltips in the popover.
- [ ] Close with the close control, `Esc`, and right click; confirm the same
      vanilla unit card is revealed and receives no accidental click-through.
- [ ] Reopen for a different unit and confirm no stale unit data or scroll
      position leaks into the new popover.
- [ ] Verify the button and popover at minimum supported resolution and multiple
      UI scales; confirm frames remain visible and controls remain clickable.
- [ ] Reposition and disable the overlay, restart/reload as appropriate, and
      confirm DFHack preserves the user's overlay configuration.
- [ ] Run `soulsearch reload` with the main window and popover open in separate
      passes; confirm owned screens dismiss cleanly and the rescanned overlay
      reopens the current implementation.
- [ ] Repeat popover open/close from both paused and unpaused unit cards;
      confirm modal input never leaks and dismissal restores the intended pause
      state.
- [ ] Leave the fortress/map while no popover is open and confirm no stale unit
      or screen state causes an error on the next valid use.

### Phase 7 gate

- [ ] Main-window behavior is preserved and the same Stats component is visibly
      operating in both hosts.
- [ ] Unit-card focus, selected-unit capture, overlay lifecycle, modal input,
      screen teardown, tooltip accuracy, and constrained-window layout all pass
      live validation.
- [ ] Mark the corresponding `docs/project.todo` item complete with the live
      validation date and update this checklist with the recorded evidence.

## Definition of done

- [ ] One reusable Stats component owns all shared Stats UI behavior.
- [ ] Both the full SoulSearch window and unit-card popover use it directly.
- [ ] The vanilla unit-card button is discoverable, focused to the correct
      context, configurable, and inexpensive while idle.
- [ ] Automated build, tests, package verification, and diff checks pass.
- [ ] The full live fortress-mode acceptance checklist passes.
- [ ] Documentation and `docs/project.todo` reflect the completed behavior.

